WEBVTT

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.360
There's always something beneath the things people say.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.100
You need to keep your ears open and listen carefully.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:11.720
What's important is to watch, listen, and think for yourself.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.550
I...

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:18.490
I want to be like him.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:09.020
Ouch!

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:14.610
You've gotten pretty good at cooking,

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:17.410
but your sewing still needs some work.

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:19.100
Like you're one to talk.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:23.480
Before Chiko arrived, Ken and Muta were on food duty.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.790
Stomach medicine was essential.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.220
Let me know if you need anything else mended.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:32.380
I'm working hard to improve my sewing skills.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:36.260
In that case, please mend my shirt.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:38.010
I've torn it right here.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.810
Hey, what this?

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:43.320
You guys, too.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:48.210
OK, mine too!

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.310
Me too!  Me too!

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:50.120
Mine too!

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.200
In front of a lady, too.  Sheesh.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.240
Will you be all right, Chiko?

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.340
Yes.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:58.650
Then, please embroider my initials into my handkerchief.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.800
OK!

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:02.490
Muta-san, if you need anything done...

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.660
Hurry and clean up the kitchen.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:09.720
Mr. Muta is always like that.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.710
Don't let it bother you.  He's just a blunt guy.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:36.190
You can't go leaving them in there forever.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:39.370
If you're slow, we'll be leaving you too.

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:51.600
Can I ask you to make some nigiri riceballs?

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.260
Are those the same as regular riceballs?

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:56.460
You need to wrap them completely up with seaweed.

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:58.660
Yes!

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:10.840
All right.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.490
Uhm, I'm finished with the riceballs.

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:33.500
Oh?

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:43.410
You did a good job.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.910
Please distribute them to the guys.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:47.340
OK.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:49.620
What's this?  Riceballs?

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:49.960
Nice!

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.280
They're perfect triangles!

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:55.170
The ones Ken makes are more like hand grenades.

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:56.980
Shut up, Yasu-nii!

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:57.580
Chow time!

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:01.570
It's delicious!

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:04.460
Yeah, it's really delicious.

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:06.750
That's very considerate, Chiko.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.930
The boss said to make enough of them to last.

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:09.990
The boss said that?

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:12.870
Was it so obvious that we're starving?

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.770
They really think the boss is something.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:19.380
And so do I.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.770
Muta-san, I'll hold this side for you.

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:02.630
We can cover it from both sides at the same time.

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:13.810
It should be safe like that.

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:18.230
I'll go draw the bath now.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:33.330
It appears that the mystery man, Twenty Faces,

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:37.330
has once again set his sights on some of the valuable jewelry of Europe.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:44.340
The items he's after are a number of royal crowns held on display in an old French noble castle.

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:50.350
That jerk Twenty Faces is so outrageous.

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:00.050
Hello, nice to meet you.

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:03.220
I'm Akine, a private detective.

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:04.230
I'm Mikamo.

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:09.350
Ah, I understand you must be concerned about Ms. Chizuko.

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:11.700
Please do your best for us.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.310
Of course.

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:16.610
Leave it all to me!

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.500
Extra!  Extra!

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:32.640
You'll probably be long gone from France by the time the next news article hits.

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:34.240
Right, Twenty Faces-kun?

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:40.730
H-How could this happen?

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:45.250
He got us.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:07.670
What do you think, Chiko?

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:09.790
They're beautiful, very much so.

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:11.380
They look like they've been here all along.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:18.640
Just as you say, this is where they belong.

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:42.330
You must be the people I have business with.

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:05.440
Good morning, Mister.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:08.340
Good morning, Chiko.  You're up early.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:10.890
Uhm, where are Skipper and the others?

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:12.690
They'll be back directly.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:21.680
Can you read English?

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:23.810
Only a little bit.

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:27.460
I can't believe they're calling you're a horrible person.

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:30.080
It's true that I'm a thief.

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:31.710
The article is accurate.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:35.510
But you rescued me.

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:42.560
In actuality, I've taken on a form that no one can recognize.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:43.790
Just like the water there.

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:49.090
If you freeze it, it turns to ice.  If you heat it, it turns to steam.

00:09:49.090 --> 00:09:55.410
People don't hold any doubts about the existence of those three common forms—liquid, solid, and gas.

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:59.520
But imagine if there was a fourth form that no one knew about.

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:01.160
It's pretty, isn't it?

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:06.910
Beautiful things enrich the heart.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:53.500
Right on time, that's just like Skipper.

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:55.900
Come, Chiko.  It's time to depart.

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:04.880
Welcome.  You've developed quite a name for yourself.

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:07.030
Sorry for the inconvenience.

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:12.230
I'm used to it.  A small country's navy like us has a lot of expenses after all.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:13.520
As do we.

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:18.280
I hope you understand but I can't allow your men to bring in any weapons.  Frisk them, please.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:31.710
But tell me, why have you brought a child along?

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:33.480
She's not a regular child.

00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:36.500
What's inside that basket?

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:56.650
What is this?  Coal?

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:58.430
It's a riceball.

00:11:58.430 --> 00:11:59.750
Riceball?

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:02.140
Try it.  It's very good.

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:03.850
Food, huh?

00:12:03.850 --> 00:12:06.180
Thanks but no thanks.

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:12.740
Captain, they're clean.

00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:15.170
All right.  Let them on board.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:16.960
Thank you.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:29.970
All right!

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:31.210
Which ones have the bonito flakes?

00:12:31.210 --> 00:12:32.390
The row on the right.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:33.020
Chow time!

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:35.600
Oh!  I've been looking forward to these, Fräulein.

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:39.360
There's salmon and pickled plum too.  Have as many as you'd like.

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:41.430
Thank you, Chiko.

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:42.390
Thank you.

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:49.090
Would you like some too, Muta-san?

00:12:53.820 --> 00:12:55.630
Have as many as you'd like.

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:59.960
We're just going deeper underwater.  Don't worry.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.510
Right.

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:04.110
All right.  Get ready to feast your eyes on the treasure.

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:09.890
That's right.  We haven't filled you in on all the details yet.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:14.340
Anyway, be ready to see it.

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:14.910
Oh, yeah!

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:17.070
Later I'll show you the ocean floor.

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:18.610
What?  Really?

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:29.910
By the way, what is it you guys are after?

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:35.510
It's OK.  Forget I asked.

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:38.230
Captain!  We're picking up something large on the radar.

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.730
Straight ahead – 1F05.

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:43.320
Distance – 2,200.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:48.450
Right on target.

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:51.640
Captain, that's our objective.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:52.790
Aye-aye, sir.

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:54.940
OK, I guess I'll start the preparations.

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:56.460
Be careful.

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:59.540
You're joking, right?  At this depth?

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:02.090
Does he have diving experience?

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:06.550
No comment at all, huh?

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:08.340
Whatever.  It's his funeral.

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:10.300
That's not it at all.

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:12.800
I want you to watch this too.

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:14.160
As a military man.

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:18.350
Ready the airlock chamber.

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:19.290
Aye, sir!

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:23.620
So then, it seems I'll be seeing it.

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:26.550
The treasure or whatever you guys are after.

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:59.270
Wh-What is that?

00:14:59.270 --> 00:15:01.710
It was a plane once, but it went down in a wreck.

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:03.590
A plane?!

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:06.260
No way.  It's way too big.

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:08.870
Was something that enormous able to fly?!

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:10.800
They never did work the kinks out.

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.750
Which is why it sank into the ocean.

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:29.430
It's good that a thing like this never flew.

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:44.000
Otherwise, they'd probably still be at war with some country somewhere.

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:52.210
Boss, are you busy?

00:15:52.210 --> 00:15:54.590
No, it's all right.  What's the matter?

00:15:54.590 --> 00:15:58.470
Well, it's just...  I wanted to show Chiko the outside.

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:01.100
The young lady, huh?

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:03.370
Come here.  You'll be surprised.

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:05.480
Thank you very much.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:10.570
It's incredible!

00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:14.560
So?  Is that your...

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:20.040
Whoops.  I guess I asked something I shouldn't be asking again.

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:23.730
Unfortunately, she's not my daughter.

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:27.020
Chiko, are there any riceballs left?

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:27.670
Yes.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:32.670
This is the last one.

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:33.800
Can I have it?

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:39.360
Want to try it?

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:42.790
No, no.  I'm fine, thanks.  Go ahead.

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:44.170
I see.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:46.760
Captain, our guest has returned.

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:47.400
OK.

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:53.630
All right.  Mission complete.

00:16:53.630 --> 00:16:54.610
Prepare to surface.

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:55.240
Aye-aye, sir!

00:17:01.350 --> 00:17:03.040
Wow!

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:04.960
You did it, Skipper.

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.100
I knew you'd pull it off!

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:08.420
Good work, Skipper.

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:10.300
Yes.  That was some good work.

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:20.140
My apologies, but we'll be taking the treasure.

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:23.330
Everyone into the airlock chamber!

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:24.770
Go!

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:25.410
Shit!

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:35.560
All right.  Here's the treasure you came all this way to obtain.

00:17:35.560 --> 00:17:37.870
I'm sure it will be quite valuable.

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:44.660
Gold bars, huh?

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:47.350
Yes, they're just gold bars.

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:48.830
If you want them, they're all yours.

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:54.070
That's a lot of them, for sure.  But coming all the way down here just for this...

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:55.840
...was a bit much, wouldn't you say?

00:18:19.230 --> 00:18:21.170
What?!  What's going on?!

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:25.210
An explosion was detected behind the boat!  It looks like it was where we were just anchored.

00:18:25.210 --> 00:18:27.000
So it was that plane?

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:37.980
This is what you were really after?

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:39.470
Where did those explosives come from?

00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:48.740
Don't think you'll get away with this.

00:18:48.740 --> 00:18:50.980
I've got plenty of crewmen left.

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:54.540
Whatever the situation, I'm sure we have it well in hand.

00:18:54.540 --> 00:18:56.570
That's the art of a thief.

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:58.120
Wh-What?

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:02.500
Surely you must have noticed.  We've scattered plenty of them around.

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:03.430
Explosives?!

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:08.460
Impossible!  There's no way you could've done that.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:10.260
You can't fool me!

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:12.120
Or so he says, eh, Chiko?

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:27.220
You should have thoroughly inspected me.

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:33.230
When you wrote Chiko off as just a kid, you were bound to get hurt.

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:36.380
She did it!

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:42.430
Return to port immediately.

00:19:42.430 --> 00:19:44.070
All hands, take your positions!

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:50.830
Twenty Faces...

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:52.830
What a cunning man.

00:19:54.140 --> 00:19:56.250
Much obliged to you.

00:19:56.250 --> 00:20:00.130
I hope to fight a country with men like you someday.

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:13.350
All hands on deck!

00:20:19.770 --> 00:20:24.910
I can't believe we gave half the treasure to those guys.

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:26.320
It's a good thing we did.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:30.680
Are you sure?  It was a big loss!

00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:31.830
Right, Skipper?

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:34.780
You know, I sure am hungry.

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:37.500
Chiko, do we have any riceballs left?

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:37.870
They're all–

00:20:37.870 --> 00:20:39.140
Just this last one.

00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:41.870
Thanks.

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:45.630
You're so mean, Boss.

00:20:45.630 --> 00:20:47.350
Ah, that's the taste.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:02.570
I want to know everything about him one day.
